<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 3.91 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 3.91 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4990 to the dollar, down from 3.4800 on Wednesday and at 1.9490 to the mark, down from 1.9400, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.91 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Wednesday's fix at -3.41 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
